infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Hand-written types vs derived types
  desc keyof and T[K] make the data the single source of truth
  compares
    - label Hand-written duplicate
      children
        - label Written twice
          desc The key and value types are typed by hand
        - label Silent drift
          desc Add a field and the copy goes stale
        - label Edit everywhere
          desc Every shape change means updating both
        - label Runtime bug
          desc Stale UserKey skips the new role field
    - label Derived via keyof / T[K]
      children
        - label Single source of truth
          desc The data shape alone defines the types
        - label Auto-updates
          desc Add a field and keyof T updates itself
        - label Zero edits
          desc Key and value unions follow for free
        - label Checker-enforced
          desc A wrong key fails to compile
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
